Fixed. The `break` statement on the old line 14 exited the loop after the first matching tracking param, so only `utm_source` (whenever it appeared first) was stripped and `fbclid` survived.

Removing `break` makes the loop iterate over all of `TRACKING_PARAMS`, deleting every one that's present.

Verified with a representative URL: `https://Example.com/Path/?utm_source=news&utm_medium=email&fbclid=abc&gclid=xyz&foo=1` now normalizes to `https://example.com/Path/?gclid=xyz&foo=1` — all three listed tracking params stripped, `gclid` (not in the list) and `foo` preserved, hostname lowercased, path casing intact.


